WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.310
A big part of the death of any hero is their
final words.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.080
Sometimes, those last words are packed with
meaning.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.809
Other times, a hero's last words are cut off
by a sudden and unexpected demise.

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:17.300
Either way, here are the last words of every
fallen Star Wars hero from the original trilogy.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:24.110
You may not recognize him by his name, but
every Star Wars fan remembers Raymus Antilles.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:28.770
He's the very first person that Darth Vader
kills on-screen in Star Wars: A New Hope.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.440
An Imperial star destroyer captures a Rebel
ship, looking for the plans to the Death Star

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.750
that the Rebels stole.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.540
Vader boards the ship and finds the first
Rebel leader he can, who just happens to be

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.730
Antilles.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:46.150
Vader interrogates him, and things quickly
turn violent after Vader lifts Antilles off

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.410
the ground by his throat.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:54.330
Vader is furious and demands to know where
the stolen Death Star plans are, but Antilles

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.330
plays dumb.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.120
As he gasps for air, Antilles says:

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.620
"We intercepted no transmissions.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.890
This is a consular ship.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.430
We're on a diplomatic mission."

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:09.430
He tries to convince Vader that the Sith Lord
has it all wrong — that this ship has no

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:14.090
connection to the Rebels and is traveling
on ordinary diplomatic business.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.170
But Vader chokes him harder and asks:

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.810
"If this is a consular ship, then where is
the ambassador?"

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.460
Great question, Vader.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.310
Unfortunately, Antilles never has a chance
to respond.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:29.590
He gives his life without telling Vader where
the plans were.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.580
At the time, of course, they were in the hands
of Princess Leia.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.510
The death of Beru Lars is extremely sad.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:41.080
She's the first civilian victim seen in Star
Wars, and her ruthless murder demonstrates

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.049
how evil the Empire truly is.

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:47.030
Beru is the adoptive mother of Luke Skywalker.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:52.080
After Luke's biological mother, Padme, died
giving birth to Luke, Obi-Wan Kenobi hid the

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.080
child.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:57.170
Obi-Wan took Luke to Tatooine to be raised
by Beru and Owen Lars, who work as moisture

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.170
farmers.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:03.250
Not too far away, Obi-Wan settles into a little
home and watches Luke grow up, carefully protecting

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.250
him.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.250
The Larses are good folks.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:09.969
They stay out of trouble and want nothing
to do with the Empire or the Rebel Alliance.

00:02:09.969 --> 00:02:13.709
But that doesn't stop the Empire from showing
up at their home and killing them.

00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:18.769
At the beginning of A New Hope, Stormtroopers
are looking for the droids C-3PO and R2-D2

00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:20.579
and track them to Beru's house.

00:02:20.579 --> 00:02:22.439
At the time, Luke isn't home.

00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:27.200
The last time we see Beru alive, she's talking
to her husband about Luke's chores.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.540
Owen asks her if Luke took the droids with
him and she responds:

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.000
"I think so."

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.189
Luke later returns home to find Owen and Beru's
charred bodies.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:41.889
It's at that moment that Luke resolves to
fight the Empire, to become a Jedi, and to

00:02:41.889 --> 00:02:44.060
join Obi-Wan on his quest.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.260
It is essentially the turning point that sets
off Luke's character arc.

00:02:49.279 --> 00:02:54.269
In the same scene where we hear Beru's last
words, Owen Lars speaks his final words as

00:02:54.269 --> 00:02:55.269
well.

00:02:55.269 --> 00:02:57.040
Owen is Anakin Skywalker's step-brother.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.579
One day, Obi-Wan Kenobi showed up at Owen's
door and asked him to raise Luke as an adoptive

00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:02.579
father.

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:06.140
Honestly, Owen and Beru are heroes in their
own right for doing that.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.099
Tragically, the Empire kills both of them.

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:13.439
Owen's last words on-screen are a conversation
with his wife Beru about Luke's responsibilities.

00:03:13.439 --> 00:03:17.099
Previously, Luke left home with the two droids
they just bought.

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:18.219
Referring to Luke, Owen says:

00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:23.029
"He’d better have those units in the south
range repaired by midday or there'll be hell

00:03:23.029 --> 00:03:24.029
to pay."

00:03:24.029 --> 00:03:27.819
Owen may have been a loving foster father,
but that doesn't mean he wasn't serious about

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:29.749
pushing Luke to do his chores.

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:33.419
It's unfortunate that his final words were
somewhat bitter toward Luke.

00:03:33.419 --> 00:03:37.819
Shortly after, Owen was killed by Stormtroopers
looking for the two droids that Lars recently

00:03:37.819 --> 00:03:38.819
purchased.

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:43.310
Owen's death prompts Luke to leave Tatooine,
become a Jedi, and fight the Empire.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:49.620
Of all the quotes on this list, this one might
be the most famous.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.469
Obi-Wan Kenobi and his group of friends are
trying to escape the Death Star.

00:03:53.469 --> 00:03:58.449
During the process, Kenobi crosses paths with
Darth Vader, and the two have one last lightsaber

00:03:58.449 --> 00:03:59.449
duel.

00:03:59.449 --> 00:04:05.230
It's an extremely tense moment, because these
two characters have a ton of history together.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:10.290
Kenobi trained Anakin (a.k.a. Darth Vader)
to become a Jedi, but Anakin then betrayed

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.059
Kenobi and the Jedi.

00:04:12.059 --> 00:04:16.459
It probably didn't help that during a previous
lightsaber duel, Kenobi chopped off three

00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:21.169
of Vader's limbs and left him in a volcano
to catch fire, which is the reason Vader now

00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:22.870
wears his black suit.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.520
Anyhow, during the duel, Kenobi warns Vader:

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:31.360
"If you strike me down, I shall become more
powerful than you can possibly imagine."

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.699
While fighting Vader, Kenobi locks eyes with
Luke Skywalker in the distance.

00:04:35.699 --> 00:04:40.300
Right then, Kenobi lowers his guard and allows
Darth Vader to kill him.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.300
Strangely enough, Kenobi's body disappears
after he dies.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.319
Later on, we learn that Kenobi can visit people
from the afterlife as a Force ghost.

00:04:48.319 --> 00:04:52.770
Obviously, Kenobi continues talking after
this line, but it's still the last thing he

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.080
says before he dies and becomes one with the
Force.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:01.849
In A New Hope, the climax of the movie takes
place in space outside the Death Star.

00:05:01.849 --> 00:05:06.650
The Empire has learned that the secret base
for the Rebel Alliance is on Yavin 4, so they

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.460
fly the Death Star there to blow up the Rebels
once and for all.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:14.490
When the Rebels learn about this, they send
a fleet of fighters to destroy it, having

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:18.590
recently learned about a small but deadly
weakness in the Death Star.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:23.040
It's an epic battle, but as you can imagine,
there are many casualties.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.159
The first death for the Rebels is Jek Porkins,
a.k.a. Red Six.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:31.870
We'll just ignore the fact that George Lucas
named an overweight character "Porkins."

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:35.400
One of the Rebel leaders orders the destruction
of a turret that is giving the Rebels a lot

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.400
of problems.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.720
Porkins is on it.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:42.699
But after taking out the cannon, Porkins'
ship hits debris, which damages his X-wing

00:05:42.699 --> 00:05:44.440
and forces him to fly through crossfire.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:49.389
A fellow fighter named Biggs Darklighter insists
that Porkins get out of that dangerous area,

00:05:49.389 --> 00:05:51.240
but Porkins is stubborn.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.939
Over the radio, he tells Biggs:

00:05:52.939 --> 00:05:54.539
"No, I'm alright..."

00:05:54.539 --> 00:05:58.840
His words are cut off because in that moment,
his ship is shot down by lasers.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:03.810
We're still at the Battle of Yavin (the one
in A New Hope outside the Death Star).

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:08.229
Our next fallen hero is John D. Branon, better
known by his call sign, Red Four.

00:06:08.229 --> 00:06:12.759
Once the Rebel fighters fly close to the Death
Star, the Empire unleashes its firepower,

00:06:12.759 --> 00:06:16.680
but quickly realizes that it's impossible
to shoot down all the Rebels.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:21.530
As one Imperial officer points out, the Rebel
ships are just too close to their turrets.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:26.259
So Darth Vader instructs his underlings to
man their own short-range attack ships, called

00:06:26.259 --> 00:06:29.990
TIE fighters, and take out the Rebel fighters
one at a time.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:34.460
The first wave of TIE fighters finds a victim
all too soon — John Branon.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.939
The Rebel fighters can communicate with one
another by radio, and one of them notices

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:40.440
that the turrets have mysteriously stopped
shooting.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:45.000
The reason is soon discovered, as the TIE
fighters start blasting Branon's ship.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:49.919
His final words over the radio before blowing
up are, quote, "I'm hit!"

00:06:50.919 --> 00:06:54.620
Tiree is another Rebel Alliance pilot who
dies during the Battle of Yavin in A New Hope.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:58.410
We rarely remember the names of these fighters
because they're only on-screen for a short

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:01.639
time, and they refer to one another by their
fighter designations.

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:06.090
In this case, Tiree's designation is Gold
Two, and he flies a Y-wing bomber.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.060
While attacking the Death Star, the Rebels
are attacked by TIE fighters, but they eliminate

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:12.240
that first wave pretty quickly.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:16.560
It probably helped that Luke Skywalker was
kicking some tail alongside them.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.759
Seemingly, everything is clear for the Rebels
to start their attack run, so Gold Squadron

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:24.370
begins their descent, and starts flying through
the trench of the Death Star.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.699
Huge laser cannons start shooting at them,
but then mysteriously cease fire.

00:07:28.699 --> 00:07:30.020
That's when Tiree says:

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.599
"The guns... they've stopped."

00:07:32.599 --> 00:07:37.890
Well, surprise surprise, there's another batch
of TIE fighters, and this time Darth Vader

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.220
himself is leading the pack.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:44.520
Vader blasts the first Rebel craft in his
sights, which just happens to be Tiree's.

00:07:46.159 --> 00:07:49.840
Not long after Tiree dies, Jon Vander also
perishes.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:54.710
Vander goes by his nickname "Dutch," and during
the Battle of Yavin, he is also known as "Gold

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:55.710
Leader."

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:59.599
Tiree and Vander are flying through the Death
Star's trench, closing in on the small ventilation

00:07:59.599 --> 00:08:04.789
shaft which they must bullseye with proton
torpedoes in order to destroy the space station.

00:08:04.789 --> 00:08:09.650
Behind them, a trio of TIE fighters appears,
once of one which is a unique TIE Advanced

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:11.800
piloted by Darth Vader.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.800
After Vader blasts Tiree, he begins shooting
at Vander.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.710
In those few seconds, Vander argues with Davish
Krail over the radio.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:23.139
Davish insists that they continue their attack
run, repeating the line, "Stay on target."

00:08:23.139 --> 00:08:26.770
But Vander wants to pull up, because they're
in danger of dying by enemy fire.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.560
Vander keeps trying to persuade Davish, even
to his last words:

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.010
"Loosen up!"

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:35.400
It's not clear if Vander is telling his fellow
Rebel fighter that they need to abort the

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.720
attack or simply relax their position.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:42.850
But we'll never get an answer, because right
after that, Vader shoots Jon Vander into pieces.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:46.870
It looks like Vander was right — they should've
pulled out of the trench, dealt with the TIE

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:49.770
fighters first, and then resumed their attack
run.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.920
Soon after Jon Vander dies in battle, Davish
"Pops" Krail also falls.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.570
Again, Krail, a.k.a.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.810
Gold Five, is the pilot who keeps saying "Stay
on target" while Gold Squadron is trying to

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.230
take out the Death Star.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.030
Krail is aware of the TIE fighters that are
on his tail, because he just watched his two

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:09.310
friends get destroyed by enemy fire.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:13.220
Krail is still flying through the trench at
this point, but he's alone, and Darth Vader

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:15.880
is following close behind in his TIE fighter.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:19.080
Krail isn't sure what to do, so he reports
to the rest of the Rebels:

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:20.770
"Gold Five to Red Leader.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:21.790
We lost Tiree.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.810
We lost Dutch."

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:26.020
Then Krail says his very last words over the
radio.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.850
Referring to the enemy TIE fighters, he says:

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.970
"They came from behind."

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:33.630
Maybe Krail was going to ask the others to
take out the enemy fighters before they could

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:34.630
shoot him down.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.680
But unfortunately, Krail dies right then and
there.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:41.500
Vader, who's now three and zero, shoots down
yet another Rebel fighter.

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:47.080
We tend to remember Vader killing people with
his lightsaber or a force choke, but he also

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.910
kills quite a few individuals from the cockpit
of his personal TIE fighter.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:55.350
And one of the victims of Vader's TIE is Theron
Nett, who goes by Red Ten.

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:59.690
At this point during the battle of Yavin,
the enemy TIE fighters seem to have disappeared.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:03.590
The Rebel fighters decide that this is their
chance to enter the trench and attempt to

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:05.250
destroy the Death Star.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.530
Garven Dreis, Red Leader, is super focused
on getting to that target.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:12.940
His face glued to the monitor, he says:

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.320
"Almost there."

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.600
Meanwhile, his fellow Rebels are trying to
cover him.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.630
Right then, Vader shows up in his TIE fighter.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:25.250
Nett tries to hold them off, but he only buys
his friend a few seconds before Vader shoots

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.250
him down.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.560
Nett's last words are:

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.280
"I can't hold them!"

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.960
Garven Dreis, better known as Red Leader,
was almost the hero of A New Hope.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:38.200
Dreis is the Rebel fighter who fires at the
Death Star's small but vulnerable exhaust

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.340
port, nearly hitting his mark.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:45.250
Unfortunately, the torpedoes don't go in and
only impact the surface of the Death Star,

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.780
which is pretty disappointing for the Rebels.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:52.280
Dreis pulls up out of the trench, only to
learn that his starboard engine is cooked.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:56.110
He's a little nervous, especially because
he doesn't know where those blasted TIE fighters

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:59.070
went, but the mission must go on.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:03.081
Realizing that his ship is in no condition
to take out the Death Star, Dreis tells the

00:11:03.081 --> 00:11:04.081
others:

00:11:04.081 --> 00:11:07.100
"Get set up for your attack run."

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.020
He's essentially passing on the responsibility
to the others.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:14.250
Maybe Dreis was going to try to provide cover
fire while his friends descended into the

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.680
Death Star trench, but we'll never know.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:21.070
Right after that, Darth Vader shoots Dreis'
X-wing, causing it to crash into the surface

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:23.890
of the Death Star, and that's the end of Red
Leader.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:30.410
With so many casualties and time running out,
the Rebel fighters decide it's time for another

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.190
run at destroying the Death Star.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:37.110
A group of Rebel X-wing fighters descends
into the trench, with Luke leading the way.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.330
It's a tense moment.

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:41.970
Luke is telling R2-D2 to fix his ship while
dodging turret fire.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:45.060
The Death Star is almost in position to destroy
the Rebel base.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:48.570
And one fighter named Biggs Darklighter is
covering for Luke.

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:52.430
Darklighter, or Red Three, is tasked with
protecting his childhood friend Luke from

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:53.560
the TIE fighters.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:57.920
His goal is to give Luke enough time to destroy
the Death Star, but the TIE fighters are right

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:58.950
on his tail.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:01.670
Darklighter begs Luke to hurry up, saying
over the radio:

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:03.250
"Hurry up, Luke!

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:04.310
Wait! Wait!"

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:07.030
He probably knows right then that his time
is up.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:10.910
Darth Vader, cool and calm as ever, shoots
Darklighter down.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:14.690
His ship explodes against the side of the
Death Star trench.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:18.640
Dak Ralter is the first hero to die in The
Empire Strikes Back.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:23.050
Dak was a close friend of Luke Skywalker and
a fellow fighter for the Rebel Alliance.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:27.270
Luke had to watch many of his close friends
die in the fight against the Empire, and Dak

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:29.060
was yet another one.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:33.140
At the beginning of The Empire Strikes Back,
Darth Vader is hunting for the secret location

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.940
of the new Rebel base.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:40.850
After a galaxy-wide search, Vader finds it
hidden on the planet Hoth, and begins an assault

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:42.600
on the frozen world.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.400
Dak and Luke, among other fighters, must defend
the base to buy time for the others to escape

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.240
and relocate to a new planet.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:53.630
The two operate the same snowspeeder, with
Luke as the pilot and Dak seated behind him

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:54.770
as the gunner.

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:58.690
While flying around during the massive battle,
Dak tries to fix the damaged snowspeeder,

00:12:58.690 --> 00:12:59.690
saying:

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:01.250
"I'll have to cut in the auxiliary."

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.620
Moments later, Dak is shot to death.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:08.840
The worst part is that Luke has to keep flying
around with Dak dead behind him.

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:15.140
After crash-landing, Luke barely escapes the
snowspeeder as a gigantic AT-AT steps on it,

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.070
crushing Dak's body inside.

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:22.640
The ever-wise Yoda lived to the ripe old age
of 900.

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:29.150
He trained tons of Jedi Knights, imparted
wisdom as a member of the Jedi Council, and

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:31.220
personally mentored Luke Skywalker.

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:35.940
He's a bit kooky and talks funny, but that
just makes us love him all the more.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:38.920
And don't let his age — or size — deceive
you.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:44.371
The dude can Force-lift an X-wing out of a
swamp, and go berserk with a lightsaber, as

00:13:44.371 --> 00:13:47.750
he proved in Attack of the Clones when he
faced Count Dooku.

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:51.540
But even legendary Jedi masters can die of
old age.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.520
In Return of the Jedi, Luke visits Yoda seeking
counsel.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:59.390
But Yoda is ready to pass away due to old
age, so he lies down on his bed.

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:01.570
In his dying words, Yoda says:

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.150
"Luke, there is another Skywalker…"

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:10.240
Yoda is referring to Leia Organa, who Luke
does not yet realize is his twin sister.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:13.530
She may also bring hope to the galaxy if Luke
should fail.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:18.000
Then Yoda dies, disappearing and becoming
a Force ghost.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:23.400
We have arrived at the Battle of Endor, which
is the climax of Return of the Jedi, and the

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:25.510
entire original trilogy.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:29.640
Han Solo is trying to disable a shield generator
on the forest moon of Endor.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:33.810
Meanwhile, in orbit, the Rebel Alliance is
assaulting the second Death Star.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.430
In the famous words of Admiral Ackbar:

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.870
"It's a trap!"

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:42.240
The Empire anticipated the Rebel attack and
prepared an ambush, which ends up killing

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:43.720
a lot of Rebels.

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:45.250
Among them is Grizz Frix.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:50.320
While the Rebel army waits for the Death Star
shield to be disabled, they decide to do something

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:54.700
crazy — attack the massive fleet of star
destroyers that's nearby.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.850
Their logic, as explained by Lando Calrissian,
is:

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:03.020
"We'll last longer against those star destroyers
than we will against that Death Star!

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:05.880
And we might just take a few of them with
us!"

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:10.240
Frix shoots up a star destroyer and realizes
that it's about to explode.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:13.630
Moments before being caught in the blast,
he warns his fellow fighters:

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:14.910
"She's gonna blow!

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:20.390
It's no surprise that these would be the last
words of a fallen Star Wars hero.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:24.560
After all, Star Wars is about, well, wars
in the stars.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:29.230
Immediately after an explosion kills Grizz
Frix, another Rebel pilot named Ekelarc Yong

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.660
perishes in the fight.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:35.310
It's unclear if the same explosion that took
out Frix also hit Yong's ship, or if Yong

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:37.430
was simply hit by enemy fire.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:43.010
We don't see exactly what causes his demise,
and that's natural for a massive, chaotic

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.940
fight like the Battle of Endor.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.510
The scene cuts to Yong in his cockpit, and
he yells:

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:48.540
"I'm hit!"

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:54.440
If you're a Star Wars fan, you may not recognize
these final words right away, but you'll remember

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:58.190
them soon enough because of the scene that
immediately follows.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:02.120
During this point in the Battle of Endor,
several Rebels fighters are inside the Death

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:07.470
Star, while Admiral Akbar's fleet remains
outside, holding off the Empire's star destroyers.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:11.070
Akbar decides that they need to do something
to buy more time for the fighters, so he tells

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:16.170
all his forces to concentrate their fire on
the biggest enemy ship, Darth Vader's super

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.360
star destroyer Executor.

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:22.760
Soon after, the super star destroyer loses
its deflector shield, and that's when Admiral

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:27.390
Piett panics and orders the ship's forward
batteries to increase their rate of fire.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:30.310
Well, something does get through — Arvel
Crynyd.

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:34.750
Crynyd's A-wing gets clipped by enemy fire,
and he loses control of his ship.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:38.610
His ship flies right into Piett's face, ending
both of their lives.

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.240
His last word?

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:41.490
"Aahh!"

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:46.650
Unable to save himself, Crynyd makes the best
of the situation and aims his A-wing straight

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:52.060
into the bridge of the super star destroyer,
exploding on impact and taking out the massive

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:53.950
battleship along with him.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:59.060
The Executor then crashes into the Death Star,
which is a huge victory for the Rebels.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:02.150
But alas, they lost Arvel Crynyd in the process.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:07.280
Don't even tell us you didn't cry when you
saw this scene.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:12.300
This was the moment the entire Star Wars fan
base hoped for during the original trilogy

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:17.530
— the death of Darth Vader and the lingering
question of whether or not he would convert

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.150
back to the light side.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:23.670
After Darth Vader repents and throws the Emperor
down a shaft, he tries to escape with his

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:24.670
son Luke.

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:30.760
But Vader, now redeemed as Anakin Skywalker,
has sustained heavy injuries and can't go

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:31.760
on.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:36.110
It's a deep moment — a father who is proud
of his son, and a son who doesn't want to

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.620
see his newly-redeemed father die.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:43.840
Anakin asks Luke to remove his mask, so they
can see each other as they really are.

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:45.750
His last words to his son are:

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.780
"Tell your sister, you were right."

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:53.950
No one, including Leia, believed that Luke
could turn his father back from the dark side.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:58.650
Even the mighty Darth Vader was wrong about
himself — there was good inside of him all

00:17:58.650 --> 00:17:59.650
along.

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:03.600
For his last-minute conversion, we list Anakin
Skywalker as a hero.

